relationship within dbms architecture and observability. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After catalogs, logs supplies what is needed to address metrics."}, {"id": "9ca52a79-437a-4ed2-981a-ac086521f0b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metrics", "children": [], "description": "Metrics identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within dbms architecture and observability. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, metrics carries the completed idea into physical design."}]}, {"id": "60005687-4038-42e6-aedd-c60d7ec9f14d", "type": "topic", "title": "Physical design", "description": "This module builds directly on dbms architecture and observability and develops physical design. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for advanced indexing.", "children": [{"id": "4a55ec3d-9cb7-4298-980a-907b3f17e91a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Page layout", "children": [], "description": "Page layout identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within physical design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before files because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "f45bb280-960a-4b92-b539-11f2d10742e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Files", "children": [], "description": "Files identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within physical design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After page layout, files supplies what is needed to address partitioning."}, {"id": "1728eb6c-e6e0-4c58-8d6b-66ba76eb0b57", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Partitioning", "children": [], "description": "Partitioning identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within physical design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After files, partitioning supplies what is needed to address compression."}, {"id": "ba971ca5-670d-40b1-8e18-1d31b913a564", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compression", "children": [], "description": "Compression identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within physical design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After partitioning, compression supplies what is needed to address tablespaces."}, {"id": "a2e5ae63-08c4-49bd-bcf7-9faac918c372", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tablespaces", "children": [], "description": "Tablespaces gives physical design a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, tablespaces carries the completed idea into advanced indexing."}]}, {"id": "772a8221-b307-460b-b353-5773f4b6d030", "type": "topic", "title": "Advanced indexing", "description": "This module builds directly on physical design and develops advanced indexing. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for execution engines.", "children": [{"id": "c48c838d-7dc7-4ba5-90ca-bdda4f180c90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Composite/covering indexes", "children": [], "description": "Composite/covering indexes is an executable part of advanced indexing; its correctness, cost, and failure modes recur in later problems and implementations. It appears before b+ tree behavior because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "1826d314-1f9a-46da-8e9e-e889e1d7332b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "B+ tree behavior", "children": [], "description": "B+ tree behavior identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within advanced indexing. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After composite/covering indexes, b+ tree behavior supplies what is needed to address bitmap/inverted indexes."}, {"id": "da225f49-3b09-48c3-81d5-f80ef58adae8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bitmap/inverted indexes", "children": [], "description": "Bitmap/inverted indexes gives advanced indexing a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, bitmap/inverted indexes carries the completed idea into execution engines."}]}, {"id": "919105f3-6e91-4fd8-9919-6a5f0b9e9f2d", "type": "topic", "title": "Execution engines", "description": "This module builds directly on advanced indexing and develops execution engines. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for optimization.", "children": [{"id": "2282cd4b-ed52-4e9d-86ef-39e9e99190d9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Iterators/vectorization", "children": [], "description": "Iterators/vectorization identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within execution engines. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before joins because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "a0226255-7708-45c7-bd91-96a50ad7c5ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Joins", "children": [], "description": "Joins identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within execution engines. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After iterators/vectorization, joins supplies what is needed to address sorting."}, {"id": "3a7d11bf-f96d-4b36-9a9b-663d4b784048", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sorting", "children": [], "description": "Sorting is an executable part of execution engines; its correctness, cost, and failure modes recur in later problems and implementations. After joins, sorting supplies what is needed to address memory spills."}, {"id": "bd832147-4da4-4b3b-b2a1-6e63c6c45251", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Memory spills", "children": [], "description": "Memory spills identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within execution engines. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, memory spills carries the completed idea into optimization."}]}, {"id": "5dccf1a7-6c03-466c-a0b5-7c12ac6355f3", "type": "topic", "title": "Optimization", "description": "This module builds directly on execution engines and develops optimization. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for concurrency control.", "children": [{"id": "f47d8f5c-265c-4dd3-89f2-969fa5a244e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Statistics", "children": [], "description": "Statistics identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within optimization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before cardinality error because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "3ecd6456-b801-46b2-96e9-b03f7da5ff3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cardinality error", "children": [], "description": "Cardinality error makes the validity limits of optimization explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. After statistics, cardinality error supplies what is needed to address plan inspection."}, {"id": "3b82544d-d591-4d57-8850-275a31ad37aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plan inspection", "children": [], "description": "Plan inspection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within optimization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After cardinality error, plan inspection supplies what is needed to address hints and plan stability."}, {"id": "681c5bbb-6074-4fbe-9dc6-e0aac865e37e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hints and plan stability", "children": [], "description": "Hints and plan stability makes the validity limits of optimization explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. As the final topic in this module, hints and plan stability carries the completed idea into concurrency control."}]}, {"id": "92d81d8f-12a9-4f90-85e7-cacabc077437", "type": "topic", "title": "Concurrency control", "description": "This module builds directly on optimization and develops concurrency control. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for logging and recovery.", "children": [{"id": "878cf4a2-2aa7-4772-a6e7-55ee9d47acd6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Isolation anomalies", "children": [], "description": "Isolation anomalies makes the validity limits of concurrency control explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. It appears before 2pl because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "602227fd-09fe-446d-a83a-5395db1fa35d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "2PL", "children": [], "description": "2PL identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within concurrency control. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After isolation anomalies, 2pl supplies what is needed to address mvcc."}, {"id": "b5f4fae8-dedf-4ac6-a0f5-64aff1b01b5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MVCC", "children": [], "description": "MVCC identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within concurrency control. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After 2pl, mvcc supplies what is needed to address deadlock detection."}, {"id": "47e5db7b-603e-487a-9a1d-7f8c65456d8d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deadlock detection", "children": [], "description": "Deadlock detection makes the validity limits of concurrency control explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. After mvcc, deadlock detection supplies what is needed to address ssi concepts."}, {"id": "d625309c-fbdd-496e-933e-dd85a0cfa592", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SSI concepts", "children": [], "description": "SSI concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within concurrency control. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, ssi concepts carries the completed idea into logging and recovery."}]}, {"id": "3d4090d5-7352-4d00-8fed-b29d919ff5b5", "type": "topic", "title": "Logging and recovery", "description": "This module builds directly on concurrency control and develops logging and recovery. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for backup and disaster recovery.", "children": [{"id": "6eac827b-15b0-4e72-a856-ff7f7cd25d13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "WAL", "children": [], "description": "WAL identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within logging and recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before checkpoints because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6ad6f05f-00d7-4e55-a7b2-6367099b123b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Checkpoints", "children": [], "description": "Checkpoints identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within logging and recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After wal, checkpoints supplies what is needed to address point-in-time recovery."}, {"id": "f2be8e4d-ffdf-4be9-b6e3-29812e296d6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Point-in-time recovery", "children": [], "description": "Point-in-time recovery explains how logging and recovery behaves under misuse, faults, or constraints, which is essential for responsible real-world application. After checkpoints, point-in-time recovery supplies what is needed to address corruption scenarios."}, {"id": "a5fdbd0e-c142-4d90-8e13-1ed69e677c7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Corruption scenarios", "children": [], "description": "Corruption scenarios makes the validity limits of logging and recovery explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. As the final topic in this module, corruption scenarios carries the completed idea into backup and disaster recovery."}]}, {"id": "4931a88d-a1c3-40f8-a371-8ca757442b7a", "type": "topic", "title": "Backup and disaster recovery", "description": "This module builds directly on logging and recovery and develops backup and disaster recovery. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for security.", "children": [{"id": "3f69fe80-3c6b-41ba-bd2e-6d8c10724f6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "RPO/RTO", "children": [], "description": "RPO/RTO identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within backup and disaster recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before full/incremental because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "9e820275-2ca6-43af-86af-9aa9ff35540a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Full/incremental", "children": [], "description": "Full/incremental identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within backup and disaster recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After rpo/rto, full/incremental supplies what is needed to address restore drills."}, {"id": "3f0aaeb4-62e3-4b5c-b4d9-3d549e95870a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Restore drills", "children": [], "description": "Restore drills identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within backup and disaster recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After full/incremental, restore drills supplies what is needed to address runbooks."}, {"id": "46b76b5c-6a3e-4029-b8b1-8d0e986229aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Runbooks", "children": [], "description": "Runbooks identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within backup and disaster recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, runbooks carries the completed idea into security."}]}, {"id": "e5f34560-9851-4fa9-a05e-bfc1d14ce585", "type": "topic", "title": "Security", "description": "This module builds directly on backup and disaster recovery and develops security. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for replication and availability.", "children": [{"id": "0e538b46-965a-4a12-97c9-d092877d2161", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Authentication", "children": [], "description": "Authentication identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within security. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before authorization because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "b6986317-56b4-4e03-95b7-8dc7b48eaa4b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Authorization", "children": [], "description": "Authorization identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within security. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After authentication, authorization supplies what is needed to address row-level controls."}, {"id": "a5ac5f0c-1123-4920-a4aa-cee875a891f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Row-level controls", "children": [], "description": "Row-level controls explains how security behaves under misuse, faults, or constraints, which is essential for responsible real-world application. After authorization, row-level controls supplies what is needed to address encryption."}, {"id": "7cc84069-7a23-4876-aca8-49c6eda2b048", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Encryption", "children": [], "description": "Encryption identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within security. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After row-level controls, encryption supplies what is needed to address auditing."}, {"id": "ffa73ba2-0015-429d-a7cc-1a9e1198581a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Auditing", "children": [], "description": "Auditing identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within security. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, auditing carries the completed idea into replication and availability."}]}, {"id": "c1074d5e-822c-49e4-b373-557961dda1e9", "type": "topic", "title": "Replication and availability", "description": "This module builds directly on security and develops replication and availability. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for distributed databases.", "children": [{"id": "24ac6a00-beff-4148-babb-6b8692e2609f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Physical/logical replication", "children": [], "description": "Physical/logical replication provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for replication and availability, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. It appears before failover because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "9a2286a2-81ea-4389-9a57-9558d184dc94", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Failover", "children": [], "description": "Failover identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within replication and availability. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After physical/logical replication, failover supplies what is needed to address consensus concepts."}, {"id": "b8ec132a-9b8d-418c-abab-e44e85783d95", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consensus concepts", "children": [], "description": "Consensus concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within replication and availability. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, consensus concepts carries the completed idea into distributed databases."}]}, {"id": "94f552c6-c8f4-419d-9ec7-163aec2e0107", "type": "topic", "title": "Distributed databases", "description": "This module builds directly on replication and availability and develops distributed databases. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for operations and architecture choice.", "children": [{"id": "eadf1e52-98f1-4b8c-a372-5ddfcca066da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sharding", "children": [], "description": "Sharding identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed databases. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before distributed transactions because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "7a75f352-8a28-4466-b7a1-4e73d281c8a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Distributed transactions", "children": [], "description": "Distributed transactions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed databases. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After sharding, distributed transactions supplies what is needed to address consistency."}, {"id": "9a71ec25-c077-4e88-96fc-57d1ec39c1bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consistency", "children": [], "description": "Consistency identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed databases. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After distributed transactions, consistency supplies what is needed to address geo-replication."}, {"id": "508c3895-ea41-42af-9cc2-6bfbc127450e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geo-replication", "children": [], "description": "Geo-replication identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed databases. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, geo-replication carries the completed idea into operations and architecture choice."}]}, {"id": "6cbdaed0-f2f1-4258-b8a6-49967d1a62d2", "type": "topic", "title": "Operations and architecture choice", "description": "This culminating module draws on distributed databases and develops operations and architecture choice. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "8b448fab-e6ac-4c14-a2b9-2f1842eeb230", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity", "children": [], "description": "Capacity identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within operations and architecture choice. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before cloud services because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6153290a-77af-4203-a65c-ad4554ec3f61", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cloud services", "children": [], "description": "Cloud services identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within operations and architecture choice. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After capacity, cloud services supplies what is needed to address nosql/search/time-series fit."}, {"id": "fbd0eefa-47ee-49e7-a067-6890c6931eca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "NoSQL/search/time-series fit", "children": [], "description": "NoSQL/search/time-series fit is an executable part of operations and architecture choice; its correctness, cost, and failure modes recur in later problems and implementations. As the final course topic, nosql/search/time-series fit requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$dbmszzjs$::jsonb,
